text:
Vera: FYI — user reported confusing examples on function-calling guide. snippets reference `response_schema` and old SDK call. can we standardize to v1 and add clear migration notes?
Sam: which pages exactly?
Vera: /docs/guides/function-calling/structured-output.md and /docs/guides/tool-integration.md. also two TOC anchors are 404s.
Hector: I can update the JS/TS snippets to use invokeTool and add a tiny TypeScript interface.
Maya: I'll take the JSON schema. proposal: one canonical strict example (`additionalProperties: false`) and a one-line "lenient" example for backwards compatibility.
Sam: agree. also include a brief migration line in the page header: "v0.x -> v1: response_schema -> outputSchema, callTool() -> invokeTool()"
Hector: proposed JS snippet:
```js
// v1 invokeTool
const resp = await client.invokeTool('summarize', {
  input: docText,
  params: { temperature: 0 }
});
const out = resp.output; // string
```
Hector: TS interface to map schema:
```ts
interface Summaries {
  summary: string;
  highlights?: string[];
}
```
Maya: canonical schema to paste:
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "summary": { "type": "string" },
    "highlights": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }
  },
  "required": ["summary"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```
Maya: lenient example (for migrating users): `additionalProperties: true` and note about mapping `metadata` field.
Sam: include quick parse+validate examples in both JS and Python so folks don't blindly trust model output.
Hector: JS validate example:
```js
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(resp.output);
  validateSchema(parsed, schema); // throws on invalid
} catch (err) {
  // log + fallback: rerun with stricter system prompt or return safe default
}
```
Maya: Python validate example:
```py
try:
  parsed = json.loads(resp.output)
  validate(parsed, schema)
except Exception as e:
  # fallback: safe default or call model again
```
Sam: also add a one-line warning about prefix KV caching and deterministic tool outputs (link to caching doc).
Maya: link: https://docs.redwood.ai/guides/caching#prefix-kv — one sentence: "Deterministic tool outputs can be stale when prefix cache is enabled; consider disabling cache or using cache-busting keys for that route."
Hector: fixed the two broken TOC anchors and removed an old `/integrations/legacy-tool` link. pushed branch `docs/func-call-v1-snippets`. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/552
Maya: pushed `docs/schema-strict-canonical` with schema + small fixture. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/553
DocsBot: Scheduled jobs: docs/link-check on PR #552 and docs/schema-lint on PR #553.
CI: docs/link-check found a trailing space in the markdown header on #552. Hector pushed a fix.
Hector: preview build queued. Preview URL: https://preview.docs.redwood.ai/pr-552-553/ (48h)
Sam: quick review checklist: 1) canonical snippet uses invokeTool 2) schema is copy/paste ready 3) migration blurb present 4) caching note + link added 5) TOC links fixed.
Maya: added a tiny paragraph about typed-language mapping: "Using `additionalProperties: false` helps keep generated structs predictable when mapping to TypeScript/Go."
Sam: LGTM. approving now.
Hector: merged both PRs after green CI.
Vera: thanks team. can someone add a one-line note in the release notes under "docs" about the migration?
Sam: done. small bullet added to the changelog.
Vera: closing thread. :white_check_mark:
